description:
In kithd events.rs TypeFilter (lines 38-85) is a Copy struct wrapping u8 instead of Vec<String>:
  struct TypeFilter(u8);
  const CONTACT: u8 = 0b001;
  const CHAT: u8 = 0b010;
  const MESSAGE: u8 = 0b100;

The live stream closure (line 230) captures TypeFilter by copy — a single word instead of heap allocation. Benefits:
1. The closure runs for the entire SSE stream lifetime; Copy avoids persistent allocation
2. Bitwise operations are faster than Vec contains() checks
3. Only 3 types exist in Phase 1, so bitmask is sufficient
4. Comment documents the design tradeoff explicitly (lines 38-44)
5. Test coverage confirms filter applies correctly during coalescing (line 1097+)

This is correct optimization under Phase 1 constraints; scalability is documented for Phase 2.
